WEBVTT

00:00:02.109 --> 00:00:05.279
Once, when many planets
intermingled and

00:00:05.613 --> 00:00:08.716
the boundary between man
and god was vague...

00:00:09.316 --> 00:00:14.221
There was a tale of a particular family.
A tale of love and rebirth.

00:00:17.892 --> 00:00:27.167
Sometimes I think things over.
It helps to cheer me up.

00:00:34.942 --> 00:00:37.678
K'Yy O U S O UG I G A

00:00:40.848 --> 00:00:44.552
This place has always
meant everything to me.

00:00:46.520 --> 00:00:49.857
It rains so beautifully here.

00:00:50.190 --> 00:00:55.296
I can dance like the wind.

00:00:57.798 --> 00:01:00.801
Even now, I'm having fun.

00:01:03.270 --> 00:01:06.640
I have a better sense of
rhythm than you'd think.

00:01:07.141 --> 00:01:12.313
It felt as though every time
I heard a certain someone's voice,

00:01:12.780 --> 00:01:22.723
I would think back to how
I grew up surrounded by laughter.

00:01:23.090 --> 00:01:28.762
Yes, anywhere would have
done as a place to call home.

00:01:28.762 --> 00:01:34.301
Farewell, sunshine!
The night rises up invitingly.

00:01:34.501 --> 00:01:39.573
It's okay, this world moves
in a way that will connect us.

00:01:39.807 --> 00:01:46.280
So that we can all smile
together once again.

00:01:54.955 --> 00:01:56.056
Don't worry.

00:01:56.991 --> 00:02:00.194
The day will come
when we meet again.

00:02:31.825 --> 00:02:36.296
The Second Daughter
and Her Wonderful Monsters

00:02:43.037 --> 00:02:44.805
There's a lot of stuff
floating in the sky!

00:02:45.072 --> 00:02:46.273
What's this?

00:02:46.273 --> 00:02:47.307
What, I wonder?

00:02:48.509 --> 00:02:50.144
It's happening again, huh?

00:02:50.444 --> 00:02:52.880
This year's station opening.

00:02:53.313 --> 00:02:54.515
Station opening?

00:02:54.915 --> 00:02:56.116
What's that?

00:02:56.116 --> 00:02:57.317
What are they opening?

00:02:57.718 --> 00:02:59.720
Why's stuff floating in the sky?

00:03:00.087 --> 00:03:01.188
Why? Why?

00:03:01.789 --> 00:03:04.958
You might want to stay away
from Yase for a while.

00:03:06.894 --> 00:03:11.565
The station opening is one of
Yase's least favorite things.

00:03:21.241 --> 00:03:22.176
Don't need this!

00:03:23.277 --> 00:03:24.912
Don't need that!

00:03:26.313 --> 00:03:27.347
It's floating!

00:03:46.967 --> 00:03:48.535
I'm leaving.

00:03:48.969 --> 00:03:50.938
Hey, we're not done yet—

00:03:51.972 --> 00:03:53.907
| said, I'm leaving!

00:03:56.877 --> 00:03:58.045
Scary.

00:03:58.545 --> 00:04:02.850
This happens every time
there's a station opening.

00:04:02.850 --> 00:04:04.318
Chapter 10: The Present
(5)/ Station Opening

00:04:05.085 --> 00:04:06.386
| don't need this.

00:04:08.422 --> 00:04:09.356
Or this.

00:04:22.469 --> 00:04:25.105
Don't run! Don't yell!
Don't break things!

00:04:25.939 --> 00:04:27.775
We were just playing a little!

00:04:28.041 --> 00:04:29.009
That's right.

00:04:29.009 --> 00:04:29.810
Yeah.

00:04:30.110 --> 00:04:34.248
My stuff won't fix itself if
you break it with your hammer!

00:04:35.249 --> 00:04:36.183
Jeez.

00:04:36.183 --> 00:04:37.785
But why?

00:04:38.519 --> 00:04:41.321
Broken stuff fixes itself
automatically here, right?

00:04:41.655 --> 00:04:42.923
Why? Why?

00:04:43.357 --> 00:04:44.391
Why?

00:04:46.860 --> 00:04:48.228
Well, you see...

00:04:48.395 --> 00:04:50.764
Well... um...

00:04:52.800 --> 00:04:56.069
That's what I want to know!

00:04:56.937 --> 00:04:57.638
They're gone!

00:05:00.407 --> 00:05:03.477
Hey! You guys need
to help clean, too!

00:05:05.612 --> 00:05:06.947
This one's no good.

00:05:07.181 --> 00:05:08.715
Nor is this.

00:05:12.820 --> 00:05:15.589
What a strange world.

00:05:16.190 --> 00:05:18.525
The things you don't need
can't simply disappear.

00:05:25.332 --> 00:05:28.902
| suppose that getting
rid of what we don't need

00:05:28.902 --> 00:05:31.238
through the station
opening is the way to do it.

00:06:54.521 --> 00:06:55.722
I---

00:06:56.957 --> 00:06:59.760
| loved that cup!

00:07:02.796 --> 00:07:05.432
Where is it?

00:07:33.293 --> 00:07:36.263
Yase! Yase!

00:07:46.807 --> 00:07:49.042
Oh, so everybody's here.

00:07:50.010 --> 00:07:51.478
Yase's here, too, right?

00:07:53.180 --> 00:07:53.814
Upstairs?

00:08:20.707 --> 00:08:21.942
| can't go in?

00:08:25.012 --> 00:08:27.047
Oh, come on, let me in!

00:08:46.400 --> 00:08:47.234
Yase?

00:08:51.004 --> 00:08:53.006
Ky OuUSsS O UGI G A

00:08:53.006 --> 00:08:54.474
Chapter 11: The
Present (6)/ Yase

00:09:05.552 --> 00:09:09.790
Wow! So this is a station opening?

00:09:10.490 --> 00:09:13.527
All that stuff floats here.

00:09:28.708 --> 00:09:32.746
So all I've gotta do is find
Yase's cup in these piles...

00:09:35.248 --> 00:09:36.516
What's going on?

00:09:41.588 --> 00:09:43.590
Why is this happening to me?

00:09:44.524 --> 00:09:45.225
Thanks.

00:09:50.597 --> 00:09:54.734
Come to think of it, Yase had
a lot of junk lying around.

00:09:55.235 --> 00:09:56.870
Why doesn't she throw it out?

00:09:57.737 --> 00:10:01.608
Why does she act like it's
all so important to her?

00:10:04.578 --> 00:10:05.879
Why? Tell me!

00:10:06.780 --> 00:10:10.684
The station opening is how you
get rid of your trash, right?

00:10:11.051 --> 00:10:13.186
So why doesn't Yase get rid of hers?

00:10:13.587 --> 00:10:15.155
Why?

00:10:45.719 --> 00:10:47.754
Picture Book

00:10:50.423 --> 00:10:52.626
Which do you like?

00:10:53.059 --> 00:10:54.261
Not these!

00:10:58.698 --> 00:10:59.366
This one!

00:11:01.535 --> 00:11:02.435
Wow!

00:11:12.479 --> 00:11:13.046
Okay.

00:11:20.854 --> 00:11:23.056
I'm going to lose my spot!

00:11:30.330 --> 00:11:31.731
Well done.

00:11:53.820 --> 00:11:54.554
Oh, my.

00:12:05.265 --> 00:12:08.001
You're so big, Yase!

00:12:12.172 --> 00:12:13.840
| can't get rid of any of it.

00:12:16.343 --> 00:12:19.512
They're all precious
memories of my mother.

00:12:20.614 --> 00:12:22.082
| could never get rid of them...

00:12:33.627 --> 00:12:34.728
That doll...

00:12:35.528 --> 00:12:36.896
Just let me see it.

00:12:37.030 --> 00:12:38.398
No!

00:12:38.398 --> 00:12:41.001
If we get rid of the things
that are important to us,

00:12:41.234 --> 00:12:43.303
they'll find their
way to our mother.

00:12:43.503 --> 00:12:46.006
And then she'll come back!

00:12:57.417 --> 00:12:59.452
My doll came back!

00:13:09.663 --> 00:13:10.697
No...

00:13:12.832 --> 00:13:14.401
They didn't come back, did they?

00:13:14.868 --> 00:13:17.971
The doll, or her mother...

00:13:20.073 --> 00:13:21.241
| see.

00:13:23.109 --> 00:13:25.345
Okay, then! That settles it!

00:13:25.779 --> 00:13:28.548
That cup reminds her of her mother.

00:13:29.149 --> 00:13:29.916
A! Un!

00:13:30.183 --> 00:13:32.252
Let's get back to work!

00:13:32.585 --> 00:13:33.653
Okay!

00:13:39.059 --> 00:13:42.295
| was sure we'd found it.
| could feel it.

00:13:42.595 --> 00:13:43.997
Feel it?

00:13:43.997 --> 00:13:45.565
You could not.

00:13:45.832 --> 00:13:47.067
It's not happening.

00:13:50.070 --> 00:13:52.706
Since you can't find Yase's cup,

00:13:53.340 --> 00:13:55.842
you want me to give you this one?

00:13:57.944 --> 00:13:58.445
Yes.

00:14:04.351 --> 00:14:05.985
Please.

00:14:11.124 --> 00:14:11.958
No.

00:14:13.793 --> 00:14:16.262
A-Are you certain?

00:14:16.830 --> 00:14:20.200
This cup is important to me, as well.

00:14:21.167 --> 00:14:23.269
| can't just give it to somebody.

00:14:23.970 --> 00:14:27.407
Especially not Yase.

00:14:36.883 --> 00:14:40.086
| can't believe you're swinging
that thing around here, again.

00:14:40.353 --> 00:14:41.855
| heard...

00:14:42.055 --> 00:14:44.858
That the reason Yase gets angry
about the station opening...

00:14:44.858 --> 00:14:47.560
And the reason she hates humans
and hides in her mountain...

00:14:48.595 --> 00:14:51.531
It's all your fault, isn't it?

00:14:52.132 --> 00:14:53.566
Even if you are her brother,

00:14:54.000 --> 00:14:59.406
what were you thinking, getting rid
of something important to her?

00:15:00.907 --> 00:15:05.078
So I'm taking... that cup!

00:15:06.279 --> 00:15:08.415
You insist?

00:15:09.816 --> 00:15:11.651
Then just try!

00:15:16.322 --> 00:15:18.324
I will!

00:15:24.063 --> 00:15:26.332
What a noisy bunch they are.

00:15:27.400 --> 00:15:29.402
I'm getting that cup!

00:15:39.012 --> 00:15:41.014
Ky OuUSsS O UGI G A

00:15:41.014 --> 00:15:42.482
Chapter 12: The Present
(7)/ Yase and Kurama

00:16:01.835 --> 00:16:03.336
Hey, what's that?

00:16:03.570 --> 00:16:04.637
Is it good?

00:16:04.938 --> 00:16:05.872
Want to try it?

00:16:06.206 --> 00:16:08.641
You may not be quite grown
up enough to appreciate it.

00:16:14.547 --> 00:16:15.849
It's bitter!

00:16:15.849 --> 00:16:19.319
Yase turned into a demon again!

00:16:19.452 --> 00:16:21.354
She never learns.

00:16:23.356 --> 00:16:25.024
Now she's mad!

00:16:25.758 --> 00:16:27.560
I'm not mad!

00:16:28.061 --> 00:16:28.995
You demon!

00:16:29.229 --> 00:16:30.930
A demon born from a painting.

00:16:31.998 --> 00:16:33.266
That's what I am.

00:16:34.100 --> 00:16:36.803
You don't have to try and change.

00:16:39.572 --> 00:16:42.108
You can stay what you are forever.

00:16:44.477 --> 00:16:45.278
Mommy!

00:16:46.279 --> 00:16:51.384
If I'm just a picture anyway,
| wish I'd been drawn like you.

00:16:51.818 --> 00:16:53.953
You're wonderful as you are.

00:16:54.554 --> 00:16:55.255
Really!

00:16:58.358 --> 00:17:02.161
When I grow up I'm
going to be just like you!

00:17:03.429 --> 00:17:04.898
It's always been like that.

00:17:05.999 --> 00:17:09.269
Whatever silly thing I did,
Mom never got mad.

00:17:14.807 --> 00:17:18.011
She would always watch over me.

00:17:29.455 --> 00:17:34.994
Little by little, she took my
demon heart and made it kind.

00:17:36.829 --> 00:17:39.465
But now she's gone.

00:17:44.537 --> 00:17:46.706
| can't go back to how things were.

00:17:51.911 --> 00:17:54.314
Once a memory is lost...

00:17:57.650 --> 00:17:59.586
...it's gone forever.

00:18:03.723 --> 00:18:04.624
Forever...

00:18:07.927 --> 00:18:09.929
Yase!

00:18:10.163 --> 00:18:11.798
Yase!

00:18:12.432 --> 00:18:13.366
Koto?

00:18:21.374 --> 00:18:25.044
What happened, guys?
You're a mess.

00:18:27.847 --> 00:18:28.781
Here, take this.

00:18:29.549 --> 00:18:30.617
What's this?

00:18:31.851 --> 00:18:32.919
This can't be...

00:18:41.160 --> 00:18:41.995
I'm sorry.

00:18:42.428 --> 00:18:46.065
We all looked for your cup,
but we couldn't find it.

00:18:46.633 --> 00:18:47.200
And so...

00:18:49.669 --> 00:18:53.640
Once a memory is lost,
it's gone forever.

00:18:58.378 --> 00:18:59.679
<i>I'm really sorry!</i>

00:19:01.981 --> 00:19:04.417
Since we didn't want to
come back empty-handed,

00:19:04.684 --> 00:19:07.020
we borrowed this
from Kurama Temple.

00:19:07.020 --> 00:19:08.054
Kurama...

00:19:09.455 --> 00:19:12.992
No, no... he gave it to us!

00:19:12.992 --> 00:19:14.494
The monk did.

00:19:15.428 --> 00:19:17.664
He gave us a bit of trouble at first...

00:19:17.830 --> 00:19:20.133
A lot of trouble...

00:19:20.333 --> 00:19:22.168
But he gave it to us!

00:19:22.802 --> 00:19:24.437
He said it was for you!

00:19:25.972 --> 00:19:27.507
Kurama...

00:19:30.009 --> 00:19:32.645
Kurama doesn't understand
how I feel...

00:19:33.646 --> 00:19:35.715
He doesn't understand my sadness...

00:19:37.250 --> 00:19:41.087
He doesn't understand!

00:19:43.890 --> 00:19:46.259
| knew that wasn't going to work.

00:20:14.387 --> 00:20:15.121
Yase!

00:20:19.192 --> 00:20:21.894
You're going too far!

00:20:28.468 --> 00:20:31.104
If we get rid of the things
that are important to us,

00:20:31.104 --> 00:20:33.206
they'll find their
way to our mother.

00:20:33.639 --> 00:20:36.943
And then she'll come back!

00:21:03.436 --> 00:21:03.970
Yase!

00:21:10.543 --> 00:21:11.277
Mom...

00:21:12.445 --> 00:21:14.247
Are you okay, Yase?

00:21:17.250 --> 00:21:19.418
Yase, what's gotten into you?

00:21:20.920 --> 00:21:22.522
Thank you, Koto.

00:21:24.090 --> 00:21:26.526
Thank you, everyone.

00:21:27.126 --> 00:21:29.028
For putting up with me.

00:21:29.829 --> 00:21:30.897
Thank you so much.

00:21:31.998 --> 00:21:34.934
But we never did find it.

00:21:35.835 --> 00:21:36.702
It's fine.

00:21:37.637 --> 00:21:40.606
I'll use that other cup instead.

00:21:42.308 --> 00:21:43.209
Really?

00:21:44.143 --> 00:21:44.710
Yes.

00:21:45.511 --> 00:21:47.647
I'll treasure it.

00:21:50.917 --> 00:21:52.518
Clap, clap, clap!

00:22:17.510 --> 00:22:18.945
Yase, we're not done...

00:22:18.945 --> 00:22:22.248
| suppose I have to
thank you, Kurama.

00:22:24.083 --> 00:22:24.851
Thank you.

00:22:27.620 --> 00:22:29.622
That's all I have to say.

00:22:30.756 --> 00:22:33.159
That's all you have to say?

00:22:34.393 --> 00:22:36.362
Hey, Yase!

00:22:36.529 --> 00:22:38.264
What are you talking about?

00:22:38.264 --> 00:22:39.565
- Yase!
- Shut up!

00:22:41.934 --> 00:22:43.169
| don't get it.

00:22:46.873 --> 00:22:48.140
So that's it?

00:22:49.075 --> 00:22:51.644
What's it?

00:22:53.579 --> 00:22:56.082
The station opening
is almost over, huh?

00:23:02.388 --> 00:23:04.624
Hey, enough, you three!

00:23:10.630 --> 00:23:14.200
You should throw away those
prayer beads, too, Myoue.

00:23:14.433 --> 00:23:15.301
That's right.

00:23:15.301 --> 00:23:16.569
Yeah.

00:23:20.907 --> 00:23:24.944
There are some things in the
world you just can't get rid of.

00:23:33.619 --> 00:23:35.354
You guys...

00:23:47.233 --> 00:23:53.639
I'd even cut things off, (Ouch!)
to prove the fact I exist.

00:23:55.474 --> 00:24:01.580
Though eternal lies surround me,
they're my safety line.

00:24:03.382 --> 00:24:09.989
"Wanna take you high?"
The galaxy shakes. You smile.

00:24:11.557 --> 00:24:18.030
I want to touch you. I don't want
to hear that it's forbidden.

00:24:19.832 --> 00:24:23.502
Moved to emotion by arguments,
| cast aside reason.

00:24:23.502 --> 00:24:28.607
I enter a game of risk that's
devoid of reason.

00:24:31.877 --> 00:24:36.649
It's resplendent with rare pain.

00:24:40.086 --> 00:24:45.157
Mistaking the real for the unreal.

00:24:48.294 --> 00:24:52.198
It transcends all understanding.

00:24:52.198 --> 00:24:53.132
So, fight!

00:24:56.402 --> 00:24:57.269
So, fight!

00:25:00.473 --> 00:25:01.307
So, fight!

00:25:08.547 --> 00:25:09.448
So, fight!

00:25:10.049 --> 00:25:12.018
K'Yy O U S O UG I G A

00:25:12.351 --> 00:25:16.655
Ever since Koto came, there's been
this strange feeling in my heart...

00:25:17.723 --> 00:25:19.625
They're stupid, selfish, bratty...

00:25:19.892 --> 00:25:22.361
And somehow I'm the one stuck
dealing with them all the time.

00:25:22.795 --> 00:25:25.197
They don't care about
anybody but themselves.

00:25:26.198 --> 00:25:27.033
| won't change.

00:25:27.933 --> 00:25:29.235
No matter what happens.

00:25:30.302 --> 00:25:34.673
Warasias, IR I e O 1 (O U1 TS Next time: "The Worries,
Beginning, and Ending of the Young Third Son."

00:25:35.307 --> 00:25:38.644
Nothing will change
until they come back.
